PARITY MAP (web → native, per the web source read end-to-end)
  • web custom popover (manual click-outside + Escape)        → system `Menu` (native dismissal,
                                                                 keyboard, anchored presentation, a11y)
  • web `<Button variant=ghost>` trigger + `<button role=menuitem>`s → `Menu` label + native `Button`s
  • web scope radios (Visible / Selected fieldset)            → inline `Picker` (checkmark radios)
  • web `disabled` ("while loading or empty")                 → `.disabled` + reason-typed availability
                                                                 (ready / loading-spinner / empty-dim)
  • web `selectedCount>0` gates the scope fieldset            → `showsScopeChooser`
  • web initial scope = selectedCount>0 ? selected : visible  → ListExportMenuScope.initialScope
  • web effect: selected→visible when selection empties       → ListExportMenuScope.corrected
  • web `visibleCount!=null ? "Visible (N)" : "Visible"`      → projection visibleLabel (ungrouped %@)
  • web `onExportCsv(scope)` / `onExportJson(scope)`          → source.export(format, effectiveScope)
  • web `useTranslation` t(key, default)                      → ListExportMenuStrings facade (P1/S10)
  STATES (every one renders — the trigger is never hidden): ready (opens menu w/ optional scope +
  CSV/JSON), loading (disabled trigger + spinner), empty (dimmed disabled trigger, "No data to export").
  The web control is purely presentational (only `useTranslation`, no query), so there is no
  data-fetch axis — no stale/offline/retry chrome is fabricated (that would be invented behaviour /
  silent drift). The loading + empty reasons are the native split of the web `disabled` boolean,
  which the web prop documents as used "while data is loading or empty".

